@@ -1,3 +1,23 @@
+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 2a154b5db9 (crbug 585624825)
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 26-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0011`). V8 15.6 2a154b5db9
+(15.6.75.88, 26-11; bugs 588740156 and 585624825; cherry-pick of main 33cdb11f68; M159 twin 51437718f5, 15.9.128.41).
+Applied as is to 15.6.75.66 (`representation-change.cc`, `simplified-lowering-verifier.cc` and
+`turboshaft/operations.h` already had FlyWeb patches; no conflict). Severity not published.
+
+- `TruncatingUseInfoFromRepresentation` returned `UseInfo::AnyTagged()` for `MachineRepresentation::kTaggedPointer`.
+  When escape analysis scalar-replaced a `PropertyArray` while growing a backing store, a Phi over HeapObject-checked
+  numbers could be unboxed to Float64 and re-tagged as a Smi, so TurboFan stored a Smi into a slot that must hold a
+  HeapObject: a type confusion in optimized code.
+- Now `kTaggedPointer` uses `UseInfo::TaggedPointer()` (keeping the pointer write barrier when boxing
+  `kTaggedSigned` inputs), and the new `ChangeTaggedToTaggedPointer` boxes Smis into HeapNumbers without deoptimizing
+  (TurboFan and Turboshaft lowering, verifiers and reducers).
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): build and run mjsunit (`compiler/*`, `regress/*`) and `unittests` `*SimplifiedLowering*`,
+`*RepresentationChange*`; the upstream change adds no test.
+
